@startuml project-a-benchmark-workflow-DEPRECATED
title Project A - IQA Model Benchmark Workflow\n[DEPRECATED - Superseded by Model Arena (WS6) | Architecture: ResNet-18/50 replaced by MobileNetV4+SigLIP 2]

skinparam dpi 150
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
}
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor Black
}

|Configuration|
start
note right #FFCCCC
  **DEPRECATED**
  This diagram reflects the Phase 3 ResNet teacher-student
  architecture (ResNet-50 teacher / ResNet-18 student).
  The current architecture uses MobileNetV4-Conv-S + SigLIP 2 NAFlex.
  See level-2/model-training/prepare-doc-training-workflow-high-level.puml
  and level-2/model-arena/model-arena-architecture.puml for the
  current benchmarking approach.
end note
:Select Model Checkpoint\n(.pt file);
:Configure Benchmark Mode\n(full / quick / OCR-enabled);
:Set Output Options\n(JSON / CSV update);

|Model Loading|
:Load PyTorch Checkpoint;
:Detect Architecture\n(ResNet-50/18, timm backbone);
:Move to Device\n(CUDA / CPU);
:Set to Eval Mode;

|Phase7 MVP Evaluation|
partition "In-Distribution Benchmark" #LightGreen {
  :Load Phase7 MVP Dataset\n(test split);
  :Batch Inference\n(batch_size=64);

  fork
    :Compute Per-Head Metrics;
    note right
      Blur, Noise, Compression,
      Contrast, Geometric heads
    end note
  fork again
    :Measure Inference Time\n(ms/sample);
  end fork

  :Calculate Macro Metrics;
  note right
    SRCC, PLCC, MAE, RMSE
    ENCE (regression calibration)
    MCE (max calibration error)
  end note
}

if (Quick Mode?) then (yes)
  :Skip remaining benchmarks;
else (no)
  |DIQA-5000 Evaluation|
  partition "Cross-Dataset Benchmark" #LightBlue {
    :Load DIQA-5000 Test Set;
    :Single-Sample Inference\n(MOS prediction);
    :Compute SRCC/PLCC;
    :Bootstrap Confidence Intervals\n(n=1000 samples);
    note right
      95% CI for SRCC
      Generalization assessment
    end note
  }

  |Cross-Dataset Analysis|
  :Compute SRCC Gap\n(Phase7 - DIQA5000);
  note right
    Gap < 0.10: Good generalization
    Gap > 0.15: Overfitting concern
  end note

  if (OCR Correlation Enabled?) then (yes)
    |SmartDoc-QA Evaluation|
    partition "OCR Correlation Benchmark" #LightYellow {
      :Load SmartDoc-QA Dataset\n(Nokia + Samsung phones);
      :Parse OCR Accuracy Reports\n(Tesseract CACC/WACC);
      :Predict IQA Scores;
      :Correlate IQA vs OCR Accuracy;
      note right
        CER Correlation
        WER Correlation
        Ranking Agreement (bottom 10%)
      end note
    }
  endif
endif

|Results Aggregation|
:Compile BenchmarkResults;
:Generate JSON Output\n({model_name}_benchmark_results.json);

if (Update CSV?) then (yes)
  :Read IQA_MODEL_BENCHMARK_TRACKER.csv;
  :Update/Insert Model Row\n(24 columns);
  :Write Updated CSV;
endif

|Summary Report|
:Print Benchmark Summary;
note right
  Phase7: SRCC, PLCC, MAE, ENCE
  DIQA5000: SRCC (CI), PLCC
  Gap: Cross-dataset generalization
  OCR: CER/WER correlations
end note

stop

legend right
  **Datasets Used**
  ----
  | Dataset | Purpose | Samples |
  | Phase7 MVP | In-distribution IQA | ~23K |
  | DIQA-5000 | Cross-distribution | ~5K |
  | SmartDoc-QA | OCR correlation | ~200 |
  ----
  **Key Metrics**
  - SRCC: Spearman Rank Correlation
  - PLCC: Pearson Linear Correlation
  - ENCE: Expected Normalized Cal. Error
  - MCE: Maximum Calibration Error
  - CER: Character Error Rate correlation
endlegend

@enduml
